From: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: run as a non-root user under a supervisor

gpm refuses to start unless its effective uid is 0. What it needs root
for is the console's TIOCLINUX selection ioctls, which the kernel grants
on CAP_SYS_ADMIN, plus the mouse device, /dev/gpmctl and its pidfile. A
caller that provides those (here a minijail with CAP_SYS_ADMIN as its
only capability) can run it as any uid; loadlut() already warns rather
than fails when the ioctl is refused. Drop the check.

Such a supervisor also tracks the process it started, so let it ask gpm
not to fork: with GPM_FOREGROUND set in the environment, gpm skips
daemon() and otherwise runs exactly as the daemon does. -D is no
substitute: it reports every mouse event on stderr.

Upstream: not sent (gpm is unmaintained upstream); the jail is
docs/minijail.md "gpm".

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/daemon/startup.c b/src/daemon/startup.c
--- a/src/daemon/startup.c
+++ b/src/daemon/startup.c
@@ -68,8 +68,6 @@
 
    cmdline(argc, argv);                         /* parse command line */
 
-   if (geteuid() != 0) gpm_report(GPM_PR_OOPS,GPM_MESS_ROOT); /* root or exit */
-
    /* Planned for gpm-1.30, but only with devfs */
    /* if(option.autodetect) autodetect(); */
 
@@ -125,7 +123,8 @@
    }
 
    if (option.run_status == GPM_RUN_STARTUP ) { /* else is debugging */
-      if (daemon(0,0))
+      /* A supervisor that tracks gpm itself asks it not to fork. */
+      if (!getenv("GPM_FOREGROUND") && daemon(0,0))
          gpm_report(GPM_PR_OOPS,GPM_MESS_FORK_FAILED);   /* error  */
 
       option.run_status = GPM_RUN_DAEMON; /* child  */
